WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.882
Stage twenty-two: another watch.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:14.609
Camille switches to a COROS watch. No third-party account: the coach talks to the official COROS MCP, through a local relay.

3
00:00:14.709 --> 00:00:21.188
One install option, a single sign-in, valid for every AI. The tokens stay with you.

4
00:00:22.038 --> 00:00:28.837
The morning check is still a trio: overnight HRV, resting heart rate, and COROS recovery.

5
00:00:28.937 --> 00:00:34.905
Named as such. Never converted into a Garmin score, never compared with its thresholds.

6
00:00:35.755 --> 00:00:41.488
And if the night hasn't reached COROS yet? The coach says so. No default “all good”.

7
00:00:41.588 --> 00:00:46.403
In headless sync, no health file is written: the next run tries again.

8
00:00:47.253 --> 00:00:51.386
Per-kilometer splits come from the FIT file, like every source.

9
00:00:51.486 --> 00:00:56.514
The watch's laps restart at every workout step: they are never copied over.

10
00:00:57.364 --> 00:01:07.491
The week is validated. The coach reads the COROS calendar, then asks: shall I send? Nothing goes out without an explicit yes, never in headless sync.

11
00:01:07.591 --> 00:01:13.111
It then reads the calendar back, and strength goes through your own template workouts.

12
00:01:13.961 --> 00:01:24.174
Race day. The MCP can't create a Pace Strategy: the coach prepares the sheet to copy. Target time, aid-station stops, pace per segment.

13
00:01:24.274 --> 00:01:27.830
You enter it in the app. Never presented as sent.

14
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:35.351
The limits, stated plainly: no heart rate recovery, no gear per activity, no course upload.

15
00:01:35.451 --> 00:01:41.333
And nothing to delete or move a workout: the coach tells you which, and you do it in the app.

16
00:01:43.883 --> 00:01:48.464
To go further: the “COROS watches” page of the documentation.
